1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,576
When a customer goes quiet in an automated text conversation, the conversation dies.

2
00:00:06,576 --> 00:00:12,277
A cadence keeps it alive, with follow-ups that go out only during your business hours.

3
00:00:12,277 --> 00:00:14,941
This use case shows how to set it up.

4
00:00:14,941 --> 00:00:19,340
It is a recap, and it points to the videos that show each screen.

5
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:27,510
This is for managers who run automated text outreach.

6
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:31,140
The AI texts your contacts and holds the conversation.

7
00:00:31,890 --> 00:00:37,125
When a customer stops replying, a cadence sends the next follow-up after the

8
00:00:37,125 --> 00:00:41,850
silence you chose, for example after an hour, and again after a day.

9
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:47,660
Each follow-up is your own fixed text, or is written by the AI from the conversation.

10
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:52,978
Follow-ups go out only while your business hours calendar is open, in the

11
00:00:52,978 --> 00:00:54,770
customer's own time zone.

12
00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:00,180
A customer who replies, or texts STOP, is never nudged again.

13
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:11,273
Cadences follow up automated text conversations, the ones the AI starts from an automatic activity load.

14
00:01:11,273 --> 00:01:17,100
They do not send messages in conversations that agents have in the messaging workspace.

15
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:22,650
You need an SMS provider and a texting number, an AI provider connection,

16
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:28,483
and the feature SMS Omnichannel Automation, which also turns on Omnichannel Management and

17
00:01:28,483 --> 00:01:30,670
Contact Center Business Hours.

18
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:38,599
The manager needs Manage cadences, Manage business hours, Manage activity batches, Manage subject

19
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:42,990
flows and Manage dispositions, and access to AI profiles.

20
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:53,286
First, create the AI profile under Artificial Intelligence, Profiles, with a text messaging

21
00:01:53,286 --> 00:01:56,492
starting point such as Qualify leads by text.

22
00:01:56,492 --> 00:02:00,200
Make sure Start the conversation automatically is on.

23
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:06,241
Second, create an outbound subject, its dispositions, and a subject flow.

24
00:02:06,241 --> 00:02:11,264
On each flow action, fill in when to choose this disposition, so that

25
00:02:11,264 --> 00:02:14,010
the AI knows which outcome to pick.

26
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:21,518
Third, the number the AI sends from must be on Omnichannel Addresses with Text messages ticked.

27
00:02:21,518 --> 00:02:27,340
Fourth, create the business hours calendar that says when follow-ups may be sent.

28
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:36,767
Under Cadences, add a step for each follow-up, with how many minutes of

29
00:02:36,767 --> 00:02:41,450
silence come first, and a defined message or AI-generated text.

30
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:47,689
Create an automatic activity load with the subject, the campaign, the AI profile,

31
00:02:47,689 --> 00:02:50,781
SMS as the channel and your texting number.

32
00:02:50,781 --> 00:02:56,208
Under the AI options, pick the cadence as Re-engagement, pick the business hours

33
00:02:56,208 --> 00:02:58,795
calendar, and choose a reply delay.

34
00:02:58,795 --> 00:03:00,940
Then choose Load activities.

35
00:03:01,690 --> 00:03:06,546
Each finished conversation is completed with a disposition and a summary.

36
00:03:06,546 --> 00:03:10,910
Open Review AI conversation on the contact's activity to read it.

37
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:19,063
Make a test contact with your own mobile number, and load a small

38
00:03:19,063 --> 00:03:24,296
automatic batch for just that contact, with a cadence whose first step is a few minutes.

39
00:03:24,296 --> 00:03:28,360
Within about five minutes, your phone receives the opening message.

40
00:03:29,110 --> 00:03:30,300
Do not reply.

41
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:35,810
After the first step's minutes, while the calendar is open, the follow-up arrives.

42
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,392
Reply to the follow-up.

43
00:03:38,392 --> 00:03:43,129
The AI answers, and because you replied, no more follow-ups are sent.

44
00:03:43,129 --> 00:03:46,729
Load another test batch for yourself and text STOP:

45
00:03:46,729 --> 00:03:48,750
no follow-up is ever sent.

46
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:57,296
The number of steps is the most follow-ups a customer will ever get.

47
00:03:57,296 --> 00:04:02,170
After the last step, the conversation ends on its normal no-response timeout.

48
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:07,636
Each step's minutes are counted from the last message the automation sent, not

49
00:04:07,636 --> 00:04:09,937
from the start of the conversation.

50
00:04:09,937 --> 00:04:14,260
The cadence is copied onto each activity when the load runs, so editing

51
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:17,460
it later does not change conversations in progress.

52
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:22,879
Use AI guidance on an AI-generated step to steer its tone, for example

53
00:04:22,879 --> 00:04:26,320
keep it short and friendly, and offer a call back.

54
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:32,132
A cadence, your business hours, and an automatic load:

55
00:04:32,132 --> 00:04:37,405
follow-ups that go out at the right time, and stop when the customer answers.

56
00:04:37,405 --> 00:04:41,788
Watch the videos on automated SMS and cadences for each screen.

57
00:04:41,788 --> 00:04:43,440
Thanks for watching.

